# Test: a static route whose interface-only next-hop names a device that does
#       not exist is skipped, named, and does not take the daemon down.
# VALIDATES: spec-fixit-static-interface-nexthops AC-2 -- an interface-only
#            next-hop that cannot be resolved fails with an error that NAMES the
#            interface, and (per spec-fixit-static-per-route-isolation) skips
#            just that route instead of failing the whole section.
# PREVENTS: an unresolvable next-hop interface producing an anonymous error, or
#           taking the rest of the static section down with it.
#
# Requires a Linux kernel (netlink route programming, and a static daemon cannot
# boot on darwin -- the interface component has no OS-default backend there):
#
# Why this does NOT assert "no interface backend loaded", which it used to:
# that branch (internal/plugins/static/backend_linux.go:106) is guarded by
# `iface.GetBackend() == nil`, and on Linux omitting the `interface { backend }`
# stanza does NOT leave the backend unset -- parseIfaceBackend defaults to
# defaultBackendName, which is "netlink" (internal/component/iface/default_linux.go:8).
# So the branch is unreachable on Linux, and on darwin the daemon never reaches
# static at all. The old expectation could therefore pass on no platform; it was
# a permanently-red test. The C-2 message itself is covered deterministically by
# TestResolveNexthopIndexNoBackendErrorIsDiagnosable
# (internal/plugins/static/backend_linux_test.go:19), which forces the
# no-backend precondition directly.

option=needs-linux

# The "default" table resolves without a routing-table stanza (it is the
# built-in main table), so this config reaches resolveNexthopIndex for tun404
# and fails there -- exactly the unresolvable-interface path under test.
stdin=ze-bgp:terminator=EOF_CONF
static {
    table default {
        route 0.0.0.0/0 {
            next { interface tun404 { } }
        }
    }
}
EOF_CONF

option=env:var=ze.log.static:value=info

cmd=background:seq=1:exec=ze -:stdin=ze-bgp
cmd=foreground:seq=2:exec=ze-test fixture static/static-interface-nexthop-no-backend:timeout=15s
expect=exit:code=0
expect=stderr:contains=tun404
expect=stderr:contains=static: route skipped, kept rest of section
expect=stdout:contains=DAEMON-UP-WITH-ROUTE-SKIPPED
